body:
@vdonato Mhhh, let's see. The problem occurs on a sub page of a streamlit app. There are 3 fragment sections with timer and 2 more without a timer on the page. Maybe too many? 

Inside the sections there are mostly Ag-Grids displaying some data and a few controls like checkboxes.

The page has a lot of content and takes some time to load.

@vdonato I found 1 instance where this error is guaranteed to happen. If you try to delete a st.session_state object that doesn't exist anymore, like In the following code:

```python
import streamlit as st

st.session_state['test'] = True

@st.experimental_dialog("Test")
def popup_confirm():
    st.write("Random text")
    if st.button("Confirm", type="primary"):
        st.warning("Confirmed succesfully.")
        del st.session_state['test'] 

if st.button("Click me"):
    popup_confirm()

```

Here's a gif of the error happening in practice:
![remover](https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/assets/73763541/f36db393-add3-44db-8345-8ce3fdde7cda)
